|OL=7561812M
|page=570
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/rnmemoirsofricha00nixo/page/570/
|text=Taiwan was the touchstone for both sides. We felt that we should not and could not abandon the '''Taiwanese'''; we were committed to Taiwan's right to exist as an independent nation.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1996
|author=Robert M. Marsh
|chapter=Solidarity with Extended Kin
|title=The Great Transformation: Social Change in Taipei, Taiwan Since the 1960s
|url=https://archive.org/details/greattransformat0000mars/
